WEBVTT

NOTE Captions of the how-to-play voice. This voice was made by the AI ʻohana in Shaka's voice; he blessed the lesson, the words are ours. CC BY-SA 4.0 · Open Source Orchestra

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.956
Song five: The 4Seas Ohana Anthem. 四海为家. Everywhere is home.

2
00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:16.541
Key of C, ninety beats a minute, island strum. The verse goes C, A minor, F, G. The chorus flips the order: C, G, A minor, F.

3
00:00:16.991 --> 00:00:25.794
C on We came home to Nimman, A minor on a suitcase and a song. F on the Shenzhen chapter closed, G on the poem still breathing on.

4
00:00:26.244 --> 00:00:35.544
The chorus: Four seas on C, one floor on G, everywhere on A minor, home on F. The world is our house: C, G, A minor, F.

5
00:00:35.994 --> 00:00:43.151
Last line: C, G, then F, G, and land on C. And nobody in this family is ever out.

6
00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:49.896
Sing the chorus twice. The words are the ohana's; the chords come from KALA's Devcon 8 floor book.

7
00:00:50.346 --> 00:00:56.537
This voice was made by the AI ʻohana in Shaka's voice — he blessed the lesson, the words are ours.
